{"connection_id": "BC-1249d5184115736d5ce3", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.5.10", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "each receives for bodily deeds", "note": "All must appear before Christ's judgment seat and receive what is due for deeds, good or bad; this is a close counterpart to the commentary's two classes of work and inescapable accounting."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f444788932cd251c9dbe", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Pet.3.11", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "holy conduct while awaiting the Day", "note": "The commentary pairs the approaching term with work and patience; Peter asks what sort of people believers should be in holy conduct and godliness while awaiting the Day of the Lord."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ca6bcb21cb3f7b323afa", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Pet.3.7", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "world kept for judgment by fire", "note": "The present world is kept for the day of judgment and destruction of the ungodly by fire; this connects the commentary's deadline to the fire-bound result of bad works."}
{"connection_id": "BC-df86da92f6a4a8d334b6", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Pet.3.9", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "divine patience delays the day", "note": "Peter says the Lord's apparent delay expresses patience so people may repent; this gives the commentary's appointed day a different role for patience, allowing change before the account closes."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0863545c14c0f286c506", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Thess.1.6", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God repays affliction", "note": "The commentary says the day binds recompense to deeds; Paul calls it just for God to repay affliction to those who afflict the community, a reversal in which the persecutor receives the measure imposed."}
{"connection_id": "BC-06f917b21c6129176a17", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Thess.1.6", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God repays afflictors", "note": "God considers it just to repay affliction to those who afflict believers; this concretizes the commentary's binding recompense as reversal for injurious work."}
{"connection_id": "BC-be0ffea2722ad414cc4d", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Thess.1.7", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "relief at the Lord's revelation", "note": "The commentary makes the appointed day the end of a period of loss; Paul promises relief to the afflicted when Jesus is revealed from heaven, pairing the same event with vindication for sufferers."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3be10844c97c2a3e84de", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Thess.1.7", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "rest repaid to the afflicted", "note": "Paul promises relief to the afflicted when the Lord is revealed; this completes the reversal of affliction and repayment in the surrounding judgment passage and the commentary's righteous exception."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5c77c78503ae040496a0", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Thess.1.8", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "fire and disobedience", "note": "The Lord's revelation in fire brings punishment upon those who disobey the gospel; this connects the commentary's fire-bound work to a judicial rather than merely physical fire."}
{"connection_id": "BC-89f5a705cfbebb68f52d", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.17.31", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "fixed day of righteous judgment", "note": "Paul says God has fixed a day to judge the world in righteousness; this directly corresponds to the commentary's named day on which the claim of justice becomes binding."}
{"connection_id": "BC-676fd4552ce2d640a7a8", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.2.10", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "created for prepared good works", "note": "The next verse says believers are made for good works prepared for them to walk in; this preserves good action alongside the preceding grace claim and the surah's believing doers."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e9dac6373f266849bb78", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.2.9", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "karsi_anlati", "basis": "salvation not from works", "note": "Ephesians explicitly denies that salvation arises from works, complicating a reading of the commentary's good deeds as the basis of rescue from loss."}
{"connection_id": "BC-086132da93b0a2291391", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.25", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "truth with one's neighbor", "note": "The commentary's truth is mutually urged; Ephesians commands each person to speak truth with a neighbor because believers are members of one another, explicitly tying truthful speech to community."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d2c0c291fadc85f348c0", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.25", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "speak truth to one another", "note": "Believers are instructed to speak truth with neighbors because they belong to one another; this gives the surah's reciprocal counsel in truth a communal relation."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9f6e7a61ebb3cc9ff7a3", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.5.6", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "faith active through love", "note": "Paul says faith works through love; this gives the surah's paired belief and action a concrete communal form rather than treating faith as mere assent."}
{"connection_id": "BC-77415403b8007ec3f84e", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.7", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "sowing and reaping", "note": "The commentary frames work as a loss-and-recompense account; Paul says a person reaps what is sown and that God is not mocked, giving moral consequence the image of harvest."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c81a4f8a977707f01a47", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.7", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "reaping what one sows", "note": "Paul says a person reaps what he sows; this is another precise work-to-consequence formula for the commentary's day of settlement."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5c75ecb25ef020d6272d", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.8", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "flesh or Spirit; corruption or life", "note": "The commentary divides bad and good work by their end; Paul contrasts sowing to the flesh, which reaps corruption, with sowing to the Spirit, which reaps eternal life."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a5b1c5137069c70e74f8", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.8", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "corruption or life from sowing", "note": "Paul separates sowing to flesh from sowing to Spirit, with corruption or eternal life as outcomes; this parallels the commentary's good/bad work distinction and loss."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a8fc2656ae1d66fe5fc1", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.9", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "patience until the due harvest", "note": "The commentary joins patience to good work before the term arrives; Paul tells the community not to grow weary in doing good because there will be a harvest at the proper time."}

