{"connection_id": "BC-3f69803eb3f7d6f4bee3", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.24", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "spur one another to good works", "note": "The community is to consider how to provoke one another to love and good works; this parallels the surah's mutual counsel and righteous action as a collective practice."}
{"connection_id": "BC-068abb521598c3aa5d43", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.25", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "encourage as the Day approaches", "note": "The commentary places communal exhortation within an approaching accounting; Hebrews tells the community to encourage one another all the more as the Day draws near."}
{"connection_id": "BC-691a1ec07b7afb39beb5", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.25", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "encouragement as day approaches", "note": "Believers are to encourage one another increasingly as they see the Day approaching; this meets both the surah's reciprocal exhortation and the commentary's deadline."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0e3f2ae8fbb647befac3", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.36", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "endurance after doing God's will", "note": "The commentary joins patience to the work that reaches its term; Hebrews says endurance is needed after doing God's will in order to receive the promise."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d67d09b0c6e95bf8b31a", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.36", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "endurance after doing God's will", "note": "Hebrews says endurance is needed so that, after doing God's will, the hearers may receive the promise; this links good action and patience to a future recompense."}
{"connection_id": "BC-19609d286424cf76c91c", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.3.13", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "exhort one another daily", "note": "The commentary pictures mutual counsel as a protection against loss; Hebrews commands daily mutual exhortation so no one is hardened by sin's deceit, giving the practice a preventive purpose."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d4e4b9e54d41883704b6", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.3.13", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "exhort one another while today lasts", "note": "The community is told to exhort one another daily while it is called Today, lest sin harden them; this makes mutual counsel a time-limited defense against losing one's way."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c2caf1a99328f083dded", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.6.10", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God does not forget work and love", "note": "The commentary says deeds remain present at judgment; Hebrews says God is not unjust to forget the community's work and love shown in service to the saints, making faithful labor remembered."}
{"connection_id": "BC-03d323e9187c249b430f", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.6.10", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God remembers loving work", "note": "God is just and will not forget the work and love shown in service; this complements the commentary's claim that deeds remain present for a just account."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6fc73d46ea40f932daaf", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.6.12", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "faith and patience inherit promise", "note": "The commentary's exception joins belief, righteous work, and patience; Hebrews urges imitation of those who inherit the promises through faith and patience."}
{"connection_id": "BC-97daf5125cfd14aecd42", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.6.12", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "faith and patience inherit promise", "note": "The community is urged to imitate those who inherit promises through faith and patience; this gives the surah's faith and endurance an explicit outcome."}
{"connection_id": "BC-dbb2b6ce434aa83d4c45", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.9.27", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "death appointed then judgment", "note": "Hebrews says human death is appointed once, followed by judgment; this gives the commentary's allotted time and settling day a succinct sequence."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f85e327363aedd398d9c", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jas.1.15", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "sin completed brings death", "note": "The commentary warns of persistence in deeds that lead to fire; James describes desire giving birth to sin and fully grown sin bringing forth death, a specific account of how evil action reaches its outcome."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2d265024aed2df1dfbc3", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jas.2.17", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "faith without works is dead", "note": "The commentary's exception names both belief and righteous action; James argues that faith without works is dead, pressing the same conjunction by insisting that belief must take embodied form."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ee1d14a6579952cef25f", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jas.2.17", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "faith without works dead", "note": "James says faith by itself is dead if it has no works; this gives the surah's pairing of belief and righteous deeds a specific consequence when action is absent."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7f4ad52ae4ecf53b73a9", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jas.5.3", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "wealth stored as end-time evidence", "note": "The corrosion of hoarded riches testifies against the rich, who have stored treasure in the last days; the commentary's bad accumulation likewise becomes evidence at the final reckoning."}
{"connection_id": "BC-53dc4491c8cb5764c184", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jas.5.7", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "waiting for the Lord's coming", "note": "The commentary makes patience a qualification before the term arrives; James urges patience until the Lord's coming and compares it to a farmer waiting for the harvest."}
